# {{ app_name }} design

This file holds the visual rules for {{ app_name }}. It is a starting point. Replace it when you choose your own visual direction.

## Where the visual language lives

`frontend/src/design/tokens.ts` is the one source for:

- Colors for light mode and dark mode
- Fonts
- Spacing
- Corner radii
- Shadows
- Motion (durations and easing)
- Breakpoints and the content width

To change the look, edit `tokens.ts`. `frontend/tailwind.config.ts` reads it and creates the CSS variables and Tailwind classes. Do not put design values in `tailwind.config.ts` or `index.css`.

If you change a font, also change `fontStylesheet` in the same file. It is the URL that loads the web fonts. `vite.config.ts` adds it to the page.

## Rules for components

- Use token classes: `bg-bg-primary`, `bg-bg-secondary`, `text-text-primary`, `text-text-muted`, `border-border-subtle`, `bg-accent`, `text-accent-contrast`.
- Do not write hex colors, pixel sizes, or shadow values in a component.
- Use the named spacing steps (`p-md`, `gap-sm`, `mt-xl`). Tailwind's numeric steps (`p-4`) also work.
- Keep body text at 4.5:1 contrast or more against its background, in both themes. Check both themes after you change a color.
- Keep the visible focus outline. The base style draws it with the `focus` color.
- People who turn on "reduce motion" get almost no animation. Do not depend on an animation to show state.

## Light mode and dark mode

- The app follows the operating system setting (`prefers-color-scheme`) by default.
- A person can choose light or dark. `src/theme.ts` saves the choice in the browser and sets `data-theme` on `<html>`. A manual choice overrides the system setting.
- `src/components/ThemeToggle.tsx` cycles system, light, and dark. Put it in the header.
- A short script in `index.html` applies the saved choice before the first paint. This prevents a flash of the wrong theme.

Each color in `tokens.ts` has a light value and a dark value. When you add a color, add both.

## Responsive layout

Design for a phone first. Then add rules for larger screens.

| Name | Minimum width | Tailwind prefix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| phone | 0 px | none |
| tablet | 640 px | `tablet:` |
| desktop | 1024 px | `desktop:` |
| wide | 1280 px | `wide:` |

- Write the phone style with no prefix: `px-md tablet:px-lg desktop:px-xl`.
- Use `max-w-content mx-auto` for the main column.
- Check every page at 375 px wide. No page may scroll sideways.
- Make main tap targets 44 px high on a phone. Never make a tap target smaller than 24 px.

The older Tailwind prefixes `sm:`, `lg:`, and `xl:` use the same widths. Use the named prefixes in new code.

## Your own visual direction

These tokens are neutral defaults. They are not a brand. To choose a visual direction, use the `/impeccable` skill:

1. Ask for two or three small visual directions with the same content.
2. Choose one. Check it on a phone and on a desktop.
3. Put the chosen values in `tokens.ts`.
4. Record the decisions and the reasons in this file.
